-- title:
--   Theorem 8 (corrected: 2κΣ in (32)) — closed-form kernel-ridge predictive mean
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a positive-definite kernel represented by its feature vectors in the associated real Hilbert space. Fix $\kappa>0$, positive sample counts, posterior/sample means $\mu_{i,n}$ and intercept $\beta_i$. If $g^*_{i,n}$ minimizes the penalized GNLLL problem (31), then its predictive-mean vector satisfies
--
--   $$
--   \widehat\mu_{i,n}=\beta_i\mathbf 1_B+K_i^\top(K_i+2\kappa\Sigma_{i,n})^{-1}(\mu_{i,n}-\beta_i\mathbf 1_B).
--   $$
--
--   The page prints $\kappa\Sigma_{i,n}$; the factor $2$ comes from the weight $N_i^n(\theta_b)/(2\lambda_i^2(\theta_b))$ of (31), which the e-companion proof (EC.45) drops. The transpose, intercept and diagonal variances $\lambda_i^2(\theta_b)/N_i^n(\theta_b)$ appear as in (32).
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: the RKHS generated by a positive-definite kernel → an arbitrary real Hilbert feature realization with $K(\theta_b,\theta_{b'})=\langle\phi_b,\phi_{b'}\rangle$; reason: the canonical RKHS feature map is such a realization and the finite estimator depends only on these feature vectors
--   - correction: $\widehat\mu_{i,n}=\beta_i\mathbf 1_B+K_i^\top(K_i+\kappa\Sigma_{i,n})^{-1}(\mu_{i,n}-\beta_i\mathbf 1_B)$ → $K_i+2\kappa\Sigma_{i,n}$ in place of $K_i+\kappa\Sigma_{i,n}$; reason: the printed formula is false for (31): with $B=1$, $K=\lambda=N=\kappa=\mu=1$, $\beta=0$, (31) is $(1-g)^2/2+g^2$, minimized at $g=1/3$, while (32) gives $1/2$; the proof (EC.45) omits the factor $1/2$ of (31)
--   - reading: $\widehat\mu_{i,n}=\{g^*_{i,n}(\theta_b)\}$ is called the predictive mean although (31) predicts $\beta_i+g(\theta_b)$ → the vector is $\{\beta_i+g^*_{i,n}(\theta_b)\}$; reason: this is the quantity on both sides of the printed formula (32)
-- source:
--   Kim, Kim, Song, Selection of the Most Probable Best, arXiv:2207.07533v2, Theorem 8 and (32), p.28; estimator (31), p.27

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_MPBSelect_Supplement_KRR

namespace MPBSelect.Supplement

/-- **Theorem 8 (closed-form kernel-ridge predictive mean; corrected: `2κ Σ` in (32)).**
Kim, Kim, Song, *Selection of the Most Probable Best*, arXiv:2207.07533v2, Theorem 8,
p.28, equation (32).

For a positive-definite kernel represented by its canonical Hilbert feature vectors, the
predictive-mean vector of any minimizer of (31) is exactly
`β 1 + Kᵀ (K + 2κ Σ)⁻¹ (μ - β 1)`.

**Formalization Note** The page prints `κ Σ_{i,n}` in (32); that is false for (31) as printed
(see `krrClosedForm`: `B = 1`, `K = λ = N = κ = μ = 1`, `β = 0` gives `1/3`, not `1/2`). The
e-companion proof drops the factor `1/2` of the GNLLL weight `N/(2λ²)`; the closed form of (31) has
`2κ Σ_{i,n}`. -/
theorem theorem_8 {k B : ℕ} (P : MPBSelect.Problem k B) (i : Fin k)
    {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℝ H] [CompleteSpace H]
    (feature : Fin B → H) (N : Fin B → ℕ) (hN : ∀ b, 0 < N b)
    (μvec : Fin B → ℝ) (β κ : ℝ) (hκ : 0 < κ) (g : H)
    (hg : IsKRRMinimizer P i feature N μvec β κ g) :
    predictiveMean feature β g = krrClosedForm P i feature N μvec β κ := by sorry

end MPBSelect.Supplement
